                    "<mark>The Joint Industry Committee re-certified Comscore, iSpot and VideoAmp as national currencies — the audience datasets advertisers and broadcasters are allowed to write into a contract and pay against — for 2026 through 2028.</mark>  The criteria, in its own words, are transactability across total households, advanced audiences and personified demographics, which in plain terms means whole-household reach, narrower targeted audiences, and person-level age and gender.  The process it describes: 39 data-evaluation questions, 672 tests across transaction types and estimation methods, and 150 million telecast observations across more than 680 networks.",
